Even when you're not a proud mother, it is still wise to use conflict
sparsely. It consumes lots of food and you can only wear two rings at
the same time, so conflict prohibits wearing one other useful ring, like
free action.

> I didn't even know there was such a thing as disintegration
> resistance... Now I know I saw a black dragon in the castel or
> on a close level, but I don't remember what I did with it...
> I didn't know they were good to eat.

Every dragon is good to eat, since all give a full tummy. Most give an
intrinsic as well (100% guaranteed or your money back).

White gives cold resistance, red fire, orange sleep, yellow poison (but
HP loss from eating as well), blue shock (which you still don't have),
and black disintegration, the most valued resistance, since black
dragons may otherwise kill you with a single breath (barring armour
layers).

Only silver dragons and grey dragons give no intrinsic when you eat
them. Then again, those two provide the most valued armour (probably
because the intrinsics offered by those aren't available as intrinsics).

> Oh? I thought Magicbane was chaotic.

Only when you play a chaotic wizard. When you play any other character,
including a neutral wizard, Magicbane is neutral. Even if a chaotic
wizard dies and leaves a bones level, the one who finds the bones
containing Magicbane will find it's become neutral (and probably
cursed).

